From: Asdlerto Korry <korryasdlerto@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] m52xq: turn the viewfinder again after a camera switch without Mutter DisplayConfig

Under KWin (Plasma) m52xq_update_transform() returned at once (no DisplayConfig proxy), so a camera switch kept the
frame direction of the previous camera: in landscape the back cameras need 90l and the front one 90r, the viewfinder
was upside down until the phone was turned. Apply the last accelerometer rotation again for the new camera.
---
--- a/aperture/src/viewfinder.rs	2026-11-22 22:04:49.531794078 +0200
+++ b/aperture/src/viewfinder.rs	2026-11-22 22:04:49.551797454 +0200
@@ -1064,6 +1064,12 @@
 
     fn m52xq_update_transform(&self) {
         let Some(proxy) = self.imp().m52xq_display_proxy.borrow().clone() else {
+            // m52xq (2026-11-22): no DisplayConfig (Plasma/KWin) - the rotation comes from the accelerometer, which only
+            // reports a change of the phone's position. A camera switch (front <-> back: landscape 90r <-> 90l) must turn
+            // the frames again with the last known rotation, or the viewfinder stays upside down until the phone is turned.
+            if self.imp().m52xq_sensor_proxy.borrow().is_some() && self.imp().m52xq_accel_seen.get() {
+                self.m52xq_apply_transform(self.imp().m52xq_display_transform.get());
+            }
             return;
         };
         proxy.call(
